    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on this August 31st slate, our offensive engine is centered around **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who headline our daily efficiency scores at 81.88 and 73.66, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside matchup against T. Gordon, where his elite power profile is boosted by a 14% platoon edge and the fact that Gordon\u2019s delivery rhythm creates an environment conducive to our heavy emphasis on stolen bases. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our top utility play; assuming he slots into the #4 hole against Ure\u00f1a, he gains significant equity from a 14% platoon advantage and favorable wind conditions, positioning him to maximize his contribution across our 5x5 categories. **Jackson Merrill** also warrants strong consideration (73.39) as he draws a favorable matchup against Singer, where a dynamic platoon advantage elevates his floor above our typical starting threshold.\n\nThe primary decision point today involved balancing the middle infield and utility spots, particularly with **Nasim Nunez** (56.26) and **Miguel Vargas** (52.64) hovering near the marginal tier. While **Nasim Nunez** lacks the raw power of others, his high score is propped up by his projected 88% success rate on stolen base attempts against Gusto, an essential factor given our strategic weighting of speed. The closest call for the final starting spots involved our depth pieces, but none were able to displace the incumbents due to the specific platoon or order advantages held by **Sam Antonacci** (60.88) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.50). **Drake Baldwin** is a particularly strong play today; his #1 spot in the order, combined with a 19% boost from facing Molina, makes him one of the most reliable anchors for our batting average and run production today.\n\nWe remain vigilant regarding lineup volatility for **Heliot Ramos** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, both of whom carry \"Lineup Pending\" designations; should they drop lower in their respective batting orders, their scores will regress, necessitating a potential shift in our approach. Additionally, while **Liam Hicks** (55.38) and **Coby Mayo** (54.85) provide solid coverage, they remain in the marginal zone. We have opted to run them based on their specific SP skill matchups, but they are the most likely candidates to see their game caps preserved if early innings suggest a suppressed offensive ceiling. We are navigating these starters carefully, as our premium assets like **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are unavailable today, placing an increased burden on our current depth to maintain our standing in the Roto chase.",
